1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:03,930
It's okay if you don't like me back.

2
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:07,170
Huh?

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:11,870
I'm just happy I could tell
you how I feel, Mayama.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,340
I won't ask for anything more.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,600
- But...
- Think about it.

6
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,250
You're like a comforting
presence to me, Mayama.

7
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:27,160
I guess I like you the way
someone likes a local mascot.

8
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,390
What is that supposed to mean?

9
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:34,800
I'm being serious...

10
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,670
So, was this all just in my head?

11
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,640
You should have told me sooner.

12
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:54,080
I've already fallen for you for real.

13
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:03,630
Summer vacation is full of temptations.

14
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:07,930
But you all need to remember
you're students of Kitahara High.

15
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:10,830
Spend your days with
integrity and discipline.

16
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:12,680
Yes, ma'am.

17
00:01:12,986 --> 00:01:15,686
Well then, have a great summer vacation.

18
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:37,859
Yeah! Let's go! Let's
go! Come on, baby! Yeah!

19
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:38,939
Yeah! Yeah!

20
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,239
Summer vacation!

21
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,439
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

22
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,440
Whoo!

23
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:45,430
Mayama.

24
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:46,900
Hmm?

25
00:01:46,901 --> 00:01:48,700
Why are you so down?

26
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,969
Come on, summer
vacation has officially started!

27
00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:53,919
Go, go, summer vacation!

28
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,020
You're way too hyped.

29
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:57,550
I talked to Tsunekawada.

30
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:59,470
Do you want the four of us to go on a trip?

31
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,220
It's summer, after all. The
beach sounds nice, right?

32
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:04,550
Ah...

33
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:06,090
Do you hate the beach?

34
00:02:06,127 --> 00:02:07,569
Then let's do the opposite
and go to the mountains,

35
00:02:07,593 --> 00:02:09,036
or the opposite of the
opposite and hit the hot springs.

36
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,676
What even is the opposite of the opposite?

37
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,700
Sorry.

38
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,500
For summer vacation... well...

39
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,680
I'm getting a part-time job.

40
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,830
I'll be busy working.

41
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:20,740
I'm gonna take off.

42
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,110
Hey!

43
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:29,380
What's his deal?

44
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:32,110
Should the three of us go, then?

45
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:34,080
Oh, how about camping?

46
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:35,379
The opposite of the
opposite of the opposite.

47
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,590
I don't even know anymore.

48
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:26,600
"After Moving Seats, The Boy Behind Me Has A Crush On Me"
(Episode 6)

49
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,210
Since I already said I'd be busy working...

50
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,780
I figured I might as
well actually get a job.

51
00:03:40,050 --> 00:03:42,479
I thought if I just buried
myself in something else...

52
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:45,090
I could forget about Asamiya.

53
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:47,690
But...

54
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:51,090
This kind of work is definitely
not meant for summer.

55
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:56,230
Okay.

56
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,240
I'm finally almost done handing these out.

57
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,950
We don't allow flyers here.

58
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:17,090
I'm sorry.

59
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,360
Sakaki?

60
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:21,020
Scared you, didn't I?

61
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,490
My vocal range...

62
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,680
Huh? What are you doing here?

63
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:27,600
What do you mean? This
is my apartment building.

64
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,300
Oh.

65
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,930
I see.

66
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,000
I'll get going, then.

67
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:35,300
Huh? Where are you going?

68
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,219
Didn't you say flyers aren't allowed here?

69
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:38,909
I was just messing with you.

70
00:04:38,910 --> 00:04:40,510
You can put them in, it's fine.

71
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:42,280
Here, let me help.

72
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:43,510
Huh?

73
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:50,320
How do you do this?
I've never done it before.

74
00:04:51,690 --> 00:04:52,690
Huh?

75
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,680
Huh?

76
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,190
Thanks, you're a lifesaver.

77
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:00,530
Don't mention it.

78
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,830
By the way, you really
did get a part-time job.

79
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:03,800
Huh?

80
00:05:03,801 --> 00:05:06,276
I thought you just made up an excuse
because you didn't want to go on the trip.

81
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:08,440
No, it's not that...

82
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,840
Seems like something's on your mind.

83
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,710
What...?

84
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:18,560
You've just been really gloomy
since the cultural festival ended.

85
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,160
Even an oblivious guy like me can tell.

86
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,880
You don't have to talk
about it if you don't want to.

87
00:05:28,746 --> 00:05:29,876
Hey, Sakaki.

88
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,690
You've had a few girlfriends before, right?

89
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:35,030
Yeah, unlike you.

90
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:43,570
I was just wondering what it
actually means to like someone.

91
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,110
Huh?

92
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:47,080
Are you writing a poem or something?

93
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,140
No.

94
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:49,580
I'm being serious.

95
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:51,849
Well...

96
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:53,520
For me, if I like someone...

97
00:05:53,550 --> 00:05:58,190
I want to be with her and I want to
touch her. Something like that, I guess.

98
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,560
But isn't there anything else?

99
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:06,260
Like not being able to
see them romantically?

100
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,870
Oh, you mean liking them as a friend?

101
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,270
Yeah...

102
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:13,370
I think I get what's bothering you.

103
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:18,670
But that might just be because
you lack romantic experience.

104
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:20,480
I can't deny that.

105
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:23,910
You really need to get out there
and meet more people, Mayama.

106
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:25,930
I happen to be single right now, too.

107
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:28,480
Huh?

108
00:06:28,481 --> 00:06:31,350
What does you being
single have to do with this?

109
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,190
It's super important.

110
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,720
Ah.

111
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,390
There's still one spot left.

112
00:06:36,570 --> 00:06:38,066
You're done with work for today, right?

113
00:06:38,090 --> 00:06:38,930
Yeah...

114
00:06:38,931 --> 00:06:40,730
Then let's go.

115
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,270
Huh? Wait a sec...

116
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,310
Huh?

117
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,700
Where exactly are we going?

118
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:49,710
Karaoke.

119
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:50,450
Huh?

120
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:53,280
But this isn't just any ordinary karaoke.

121
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,440
Sakaki.

122
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,440
Oh.

123
00:06:56,550 --> 00:06:57,280
Don't tell me this is...

124
00:06:57,380 --> 00:06:58,810
A mixer at karaoke!

125
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,650
You didn't tell me it was this!

126
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:02,529
Didn't you want to understand women?

127
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:04,150
I never said that!

128
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:05,990
Alright, alright, alright.

129
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:06,490
I'm...

130
00:07:06,491 --> 00:07:08,360
Huh? Isn't that Sakaki and Mayama?

131
00:07:09,830 --> 00:07:11,390
Asamiya...

132
00:07:11,990 --> 00:07:12,930
What are you guys doing?

133
00:07:12,931 --> 00:07:14,100
Just hanging out.

134
00:07:14,290 --> 00:07:14,930
What about you?

135
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:15,930
Isn't it obvious?

136
00:07:15,930 --> 00:07:16,930
Ah... wait a minute.

137
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:18,100
A mixer.

138
00:07:18,101 --> 00:07:19,940
You really love these things, Sakaki.

139
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:21,669
Which means Mayama is...

140
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:22,560
No, I'm...

141
00:07:22,561 --> 00:07:26,070
Mayama insisted on coming.
He wouldn't take no for an answer.

142
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:28,350
Let's go.

143
00:07:33,710 --> 00:07:34,710
Come on, come on.

144
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:36,520
Get in, get in!

145
00:07:39,370 --> 00:07:40,120
What are you doing?

146
00:07:40,121 --> 00:07:41,320
Ah, wait a sec!

147
00:07:52,170 --> 00:07:54,939
Thanks!

148
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:57,240
Nice to meet you all today.

149
00:07:58,430 --> 00:08:00,040
Great singing!

150
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:01,650
Here.

151
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:03,250
Introduce yourself and pick a song.

152
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:04,550
Huh?

153
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:05,680
Ah...

154
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:08,290
Here you go.

155
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,460
I'm Mayama.

156
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,300
That's it.

157
00:08:26,570 --> 00:08:28,770
As for a song... maybe later.

158
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,910
Next, then!

159
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:41,020
Asamiya definitely got the wrong idea.

160
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:45,120
Thanks for waiting.
Here's your iced coffee.

161
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:49,490
You really surprised me earlier.

162
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,890
I never thought you'd
go to a mixer, Mayama.

163
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,100
Sorry for calling you out of the blue.

164
00:08:57,830 --> 00:08:59,200
I was a little surprised.

165
00:08:59,390 --> 00:09:02,400
After all, this is the first time
you've come to me for advice.

166
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:04,770
So, what's up?

167
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:10,180
There's someone I like.

168
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,020
Hmm...

169
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,120
You're not surprised?

170
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:17,690
Huh?

171
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:20,690
No, I am surprised.

172
00:09:20,750 --> 00:09:23,590
Because I've never heard you
talk about this kind of thing before.

173
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:25,370
Yeah.

174
00:09:25,430 --> 00:09:26,430
So...

175
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:27,730
What kind of person are they?

176
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:32,070
They're really kind.

177
00:09:33,690 --> 00:09:38,970
They always put other people's
feelings before his own.

178
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,640
Yeah.

179
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:45,010
Before I knew it, I had
already fallen for them.

180
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,650
I even told them how I felt.

181
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:51,410
But...

182
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:54,720
They didn't like you back?

183
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:01,760
I was the one who said it was
okay if they didn't like me back.

184
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:04,570
What do you mean?

185
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,670
Because they're a kind person.

186
00:10:11,890 --> 00:10:13,280
Too kind.

187
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:20,480
I think right now, he's trying desperately
to respond to everyone's feelings.

188
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:25,720
Thinking they have to like
me back for my sake.

189
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:28,860
Something like that.

190
00:10:32,530 --> 00:10:35,290
There might come a day when they
just force themselves to accommodate me.

191
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:37,900
That wouldn't work, right?

192
00:10:39,710 --> 00:10:43,240
Because that's not what I want.

193
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:51,650
If he genuinely fell for
me, of course I'd be happy.

194
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:54,420
But if that's not the case...

195
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:57,470
Then...

196
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:03,540
It wouldn't be his true feelings,
which is what I really want.

197
00:11:05,350 --> 00:11:06,350
So...

198
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,270
You're dealing with a
pretty tough romance, huh.

199
00:11:17,570 --> 00:11:18,570
Huh?

200
00:11:18,790 --> 00:11:19,610
No, it's just...

201
00:11:19,740 --> 00:11:23,220
I just suddenly realized that you worry about
these things just like any normal person.

202
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:25,656
I'm seriously asking for your advice here.

203
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:26,880
My bad, my bad.

204
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:28,120
But seriously,

205
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:30,746
it's my first time talking to
someone about this kind of thing.

206
00:11:30,770 --> 00:11:31,770
It's super embarrassing.

207
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:35,360
I'm actually glad to see this side of you.

208
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,360
Huh?

209
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:40,600
Why don't you just show that
person this side of you too?

210
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:43,000
Everything you just said,

211
00:11:43,350 --> 00:11:45,230
all those confusing feelings you have,

212
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:49,040
if you just tell them properly,
they'll definitely understand.

213
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,710
Or do you not trust them?

214
00:11:57,350 --> 00:11:59,410
You don't trust the
person you've fallen for?

215
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,480
It's not that.

216
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:07,820
I'd really love to meet them.

217
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:11,190
What kind of person could make
Asamiya fall so hard?

218
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:15,230
Ah...

219
00:12:17,830 --> 00:12:18,830
Yeah.

220
00:12:23,310 --> 00:12:24,470
Mayama.

221
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,570
Anyway, I'm rooting for you.

222
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,360
Nice singing.

223
00:13:17,361 --> 00:13:18,820
Really?

224
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:22,600
That was awesome.

225
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:25,479
What made you choose this song?

226
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,646
I'm gonna go to the restroom...

227
00:13:26,670 --> 00:13:28,140
Don't be jealous.

228
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,139
- His pronunciation was spot on.
- No way.

229
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:31,140
Um...

230
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,460
I thought he was American.

231
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,559
I know, right?

232
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,680
It suddenly makes me
want to fly overseas for a trip.

233
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:42,749
By the way, that guy we ran into
earlier who seemed like Sakaki's friend...

234
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:43,550
Yeah?

235
00:13:43,551 --> 00:13:44,859
His name is Asamiya, right?

236
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:46,139
He's super hot, isn't he?

237
00:13:46,163 --> 00:13:46,712
Totally.

238
00:13:46,736 --> 00:13:49,013
He's on a whole other level. I think I'm a little in love.

239
00:13:49,690 --> 00:13:51,229
Don't you have a boyfriend?

240
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:53,700
How should I put it?
He's in a different category.

241
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,019
Huh? Why are you even at a mixer then?

242
00:13:56,020 --> 00:14:00,670
There's no way Asamiya could
actually like someone like me.

243
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,610
It was impossible from the very beginning.

244
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:05,210
I came here today behind his back.

245
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,309
Then just find someone else today.

246
00:14:07,310 --> 00:14:08,310
Oh.

247
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,980
What are you doing here?

248
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,020
I came looking for you.

249
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,580
For me?

250
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:17,520
Yeah. And after I found you,

251
00:14:17,650 --> 00:14:20,770
you were just standing here frozen for
some reason, so I was just watching you.

252
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:24,960
Wait a minute.

253
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,600
Go home.

254
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:36,970
Weren't you the one
who drew the line first, Asamiya?

255
00:14:44,850 --> 00:14:47,280
- Oh, welcome back.
- Welcome back.

256
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:49,160
Here.

257
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,290
It's about time Mayama sang a song too.

258
00:14:52,650 --> 00:14:53,650
Yeah.

259
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:55,339
Huh? Seriously?

260
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,699
Can you sing?

261
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:58,319
What are you gonna sing?

262
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,080
- Sing a Western song.
- Stop messing around.

263
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:05,670
Asamiya?

264
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,500
It's that hot guy from earlier.

265
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,200
Let's go.

266
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:15,520
What's going on?

267
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:25,450
Did you have fun at the mixer?

268
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:28,590
I was just dragged there.

269
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:35,030
Sakaki sure is lucky.
He gets to put his arm around you.

270
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:54,320
Have you ever done this with Sakaki?

271
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,820
Of course not.

272
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:06,060
What about this?

273
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:15,200
How does it feel to have
me hold your hand like this?

274
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,510
I don't know.

275
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,080
I've never done anything like this before.

276
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,020
But you're blushing.

277
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:43,530
I haven't been able to see
you since summer break started.

278
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:47,300
I've been so frustrated.

279
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:54,240
I've been wanting to do this, to really
feel that you're right here beside me.

280
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:01,320
You're so unfair.

281
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:07,960
When you say things like that,
what am I supposed to do?

282
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:11,130
I don't understand you at all, Asamiya.

283
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,170
You were the one who drew the line first.

284
00:17:20,170 --> 00:17:22,340
So don't just cross it again.

285
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:25,740
I'm sorry.

286
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,410
In my own way, I was...

287
00:17:32,410 --> 00:17:36,750
thinking really seriously
about you, Asamiya.

288
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:44,230
Though someone as perfect as you
probably wouldn't understand how I feel.

289
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,330
I'm not perfect at all.

290
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,360
Huh?

291
00:17:58,370 --> 00:18:00,240
You heard them earlier, right?

292
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:07,820
My whole life has been like that.
People only judge me by my looks.

293
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:15,000
People have high expectations, but the moment
I fail, they're quick to sneer and say,

294
00:18:15,089 --> 00:18:16,989
"He's just a pretty face after all."

295
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:24,570
That's why I've always tried so hard.

296
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:29,550
To be honest, I'm panicking right now too.

297
00:18:31,850 --> 00:18:36,280
The overwhelming happiness of being with you
that makes me feel like I'm losing control,

298
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:40,650
the desire to not hurt you,

299
00:18:42,230 --> 00:18:44,220
the urge to clear up the misunderstanding,

300
00:18:46,090 --> 00:18:47,730
all these feelings are mixed up together.

301
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:52,330
Even so,

302
00:18:53,530 --> 00:18:55,760
I still want to look cool in front of you.

303
00:18:58,490 --> 00:19:01,490
I always end up unconsciously acting
like I've got everything under control.

304
00:19:05,090 --> 00:19:07,610
What misunderstanding...
are you talking about?

305
00:19:13,470 --> 00:19:16,390
You're not some local mascot.

306
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:25,630
If you didn't actually like me, Mayama,

307
00:19:26,230 --> 00:19:29,560
but forced yourself to like me to
spare my feelings, that would really hurt.

308
00:19:30,690 --> 00:19:32,000
That's why I said those things.

309
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:34,500
Eh...

310
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:36,730
But...

311
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:40,040
I was completely wrong.

312
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:42,440
I'm sorry.

313
00:19:47,470 --> 00:19:52,890
So... when you said you liked me before,

314
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:57,790
it wasn't just as a friend, but...

315
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:02,860
Of course I meant it romantically.

316
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,100
I want to hold your hand.

317
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:14,240
I want to hug you, and...

318
00:20:17,990 --> 00:20:20,050
I want to spend more time with you, Mayama.

319
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,160
Mayama?

320
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:38,700
Thank goodness...

321
00:20:43,610 --> 00:20:45,810
I thought... it was already hopeless.

322
00:20:48,110 --> 00:20:49,110
I'm sorry.

323
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:54,850
I would never force myself to like you
just to spare your feelings, Asamiya.

324
00:20:57,410 --> 00:20:59,290
So please don't draw that line again.

325
00:21:02,480 --> 00:21:03,480
Okay.

326
00:21:07,530 --> 00:21:11,700
Because I like you, Asamiya.

327
00:21:16,930 --> 00:21:18,570
What kind of "like"?

328
00:21:20,310 --> 00:21:21,310
Huh?

329
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:26,280
I feel like I've made
my feelings pretty clear.

330
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:30,950
So I want to hear it from you too, Mayama.

331
00:21:32,630 --> 00:21:33,890
Your "like"...

332
00:21:35,470 --> 00:21:36,830
What kind of "like" is it?

333
00:21:45,690 --> 00:21:49,240
I want to touch you.

334
00:21:55,870 --> 00:21:58,450
I want to hold your hand too.

335
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:01,510
I want to hug you.

336
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:04,590
It's that kind of "like."

337
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:15,760
I'm sorry.

338
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,640
It's okay.

339
00:22:24,190 --> 00:22:25,870
I don't hate it.

340
00:22:33,330 --> 00:22:34,550
Your phone is ringing.

341
00:23:12,950 --> 00:23:14,990
I really want to see you soon.

342
00:23:16,070 --> 00:23:17,360
Kou-chan.

343
00:24:41,550 --> 00:24:42,826
(Next Episode)
Hi, I'm his boyfriend.

344
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:43,850
I know.

345
00:24:44,310 --> 00:24:45,826
(Tanabata Festival)
Do you want to go together?

346
00:24:45,850 --> 00:24:47,609
It'd be nice if we could do something
that feels like summer.

347
00:24:47,610 --> 00:24:50,489
I didn't expect it to be
an event part-time job.

348
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:51,490
Kou-chan.

349
00:24:52,310 --> 00:24:55,290
What's her relationship with Asamiya?
